course: dictionary
lesson: 15371
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Soy is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it, because they are its context. «Dan poured soy milk over his cereal» has the clue milk, so soy must mean made from soya.
explain: «Mum added a splash of soy sauce to the noodles.» The word sauce tells you that soy means the dark, salty sauce. Check by swapping in your meaning: a dark, salty sauce made from soya beans fits the sentence.
explain: Soy can also mean the beans themselves. «Soy beans are the seeds of a plant from East Asia, and they are rich in protein.» Here the sentence tells you the soy is the seeds, not a sauce or a drink.
explain: Food labels are a useful clue too. «Contains soy» on a packet means soy is in the food. Soy is a common allergen, so the label warns people who must avoid it.
fact: «Soy» can be a noun (the beans, or the sauce) or an adjective (made from soya).
fact: «Soy» means soya beans, the seeds of a plant from East Asia.
fact: «Soy sauce» means a dark, salty sauce made from fermented soya beans.
fact: «Soy milk» and «soy yoghurt» are made from soya.
fact: Soy is a common allergen, so food labels often warn about it.
exercise: «Dan poured soy milk over his cereal.» What is soy milk? | *Milk made from soya | A sweet made from sugar | Milk from a cow in a field | Juice squeezed from oranges
exercise: «Mum added a splash of soy sauce to the noodles.» What is soy sauce? | *A dark, salty sauce made from fermented soya beans | A sweet, sticky syrup for pancakes | A thick cream for cakes | A cold fruit drink
exercise: «Soy is the seeds of a plant from East Asia.» What does soy mean here? | A kind of cheese | A small fish | *Soya beans | A type of tree
test: What does soy mean in «Ella's yoghurt is soy yoghurt, made from soya»? | Very sweet and frozen | Made from soya | Made from cows' milk | *Made from soya, as in soy yoghurt
test: «Huge fields in Brazil and the USA grow soy.» What is grown there? | Only rice | Tea | *Soya plants | Potatoes
exam: Why might «Contains soy» be printed on a food packet? | *Soy is a common allergen, so people who must avoid it need to know | Soy is a kind of cloud, so the packet is showing the weather | Soy is a type of fish | Labels only list colours
